{
 "_about": "Enemies for the combat sandbox (docs/pivot/combat_api.md 4.2). Numbers are starting guesses for Ross to tune. 'model' is tried first, then 'fallback_model', then a coloured blockout (capsule or box) so nothing is ever missing.",
 "version": 1,
 "max_attackers": 2,
 "token_rules": {
  "_about": "enemy_ai_design 5. Defending and fleeing enemies hold no token (they do not ask). Two hits never land closer than min_impact_gap_ms. Only max_rear_attackers enemy may attack from Red's rear arc (rear_arc_deg wide, centred behind her). A flanker queues as if it had waited flanker_queue_bonus_ms longer. The 'Enemies attacking at once' feel knob (enemy_max_attackers) overrides max_attackers.",
  "min_impact_gap_ms": 450,
  "max_rear_attackers": 1,
  "rear_arc_deg": 120,
  "flanker_queue_bonus_ms": 1500,
  "max_flankers": 1,
  "defending_holds_token": false,
  "fleeing_holds_token": false
 },
 "telegraph_rules": {
  "_about": "enemy_ai_design 4. Every attack: at least min_windup_ms from telegraph to impact (rear_min_windup_ms when the attacker stands in Red's rear arc), and the aim locks at least min_aim_lock_before_impact_ms before impact. The 'Attack wind-up length' knob can only make wind-ups longer. tests/unit/test_enemy_ai_data.gd checks every enemy attack against these.",
  "min_windup_ms": 500,
  "rear_min_windup_ms": 650,
  "min_aim_lock_before_impact_ms": 150,
  "rear_arc_deg": 120
 },
 "play_bounds": {
  "_about": "B8 safety net. An enemy that leaves the playable space (physics blow-up, bad launch) is taken out of play cleanly and counted as defeated, instead of flying off and flooding the log. All distances are from the enemy's spawn spot. kill_below_spawn_m: lower than this (negative) is below the floor; ceiling_above_spawn_m: higher than this is above the level; max_from_spawn_m: further than this sideways is out of the arena. spawn_gap_m: extra space left when an enemy spawned on top of an ally steps clear of it.",
  "kill_below_spawn_m": -30.0,
  "ceiling_above_spawn_m": 60.0,
  "max_from_spawn_m": 300.0,
  "spawn_gap_m": 0.1
 },
 "player_read": {
  "_about": "How enemies read Red: her move as a class (light / heavy / launcher / air; a move not listed here is classed from its own data), how long a string of her hits stays 'a combo', and what counts as a dash toward an enemy.",
